          "heading": false
        }
      ],
      "extract": "Our mechanical model of fat knots is constructed from a ﬂexible but re- silient hollow rectilinear metallic cylinder of length 50 cm and diameter 2mm. If one bends the cylinder and places it on a table, it straightens out almost in- stantly (after some oscilliations) and reacquires its original rectilinear shape; if one bends it so that several loops are formed and the cylinder is released, it will jump up slightly",
      "extractCut": true
