      ],
      "extract": "Recall that the winding number (or Whitney index) w(C) of a smooth regular curve C in the plane is the number of revolutions that its tangent vector performs when we go around the curve. To every initial position M of our mechanical knot on the table, we can associate a smooth planar curve 7 CM, the projection of the smooth curve in space constituting the core (cen- tral curve) of M onto the plane of the table.",
      "extractCut": true
