      "extract": "In observing the evolution of the shape of mechanical knots, we were able to notice that the device actually performs certain local moves well known in classical knot theory. In particular, mechanical knots can (under appropriate “boundary conditions”): • perform the ﬁrst Reidemeister move Ω1 in both directions; we have already seen that our device immediately gets rid of little loops, but it can also create a loop:",
